.TH EUCLID-CLI-EQS-DELETE-QUEUE-TAG 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eqs-delete-queue-tag \- delete a tag from a queue
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli eqs delete-queue-tag
.BR \-\-queue | \-q
.I ERN
.BR \-\-key | \-k
.I KEY
.SH DESCRIPTION
Deletes a tag from a queue identified by its Euclid resource name (ERN).
Deleting a key that has no matching tag is not an error.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-queue " " \fIERN\fR
Euclid resource name of the queue. Required.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-key " " \fIKEY\fR
Key of the tag to delete. Required.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The tag was deleted (or was already absent). No output is printed.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the server could not be reached, or no queue
with that ERN exists.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eqs delete-queue-tag \e
    --queue ern:eqs:eu-central-1:000000000000:queue:orders --key team
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eqs (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-add-queue-tag (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-set-queue-tag (1)
